{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Lamekh lived two and eighty years and a hundred years.</b> You will find in the reckoning from Adam to Noah one thousand and fifty-six (אלף נ\"ו) years if you count the years of all the generations: for Adam was one hundred and thirty (ק\"ל) years old when he begot Shet, one hundred and five (ק\"ה) years for Shet when he begot Enosh, ninety (צ') years for Enosh when he begot Qenan, seventy (ע') for Qenan when he begot Mahalalel, sixty-five (ס\"ה) for Mahalalel when he begot Yered, one hundred and sixty-two (קס\"ב) years for Yered when he begot Hanokh, sixty-five (ס\"ה) years for Hanokh when he begot Metushelakh, one hundred and eighty-seven (קפ\"ז) years for Metushelakh when he begot Lamekh, one hundred and eighty-two (קפ\"ב) years for Lamekh when he begot Noah — and this reckoning comes out precisely to one thousand and fifty-six (אלף נ\"ו) years from Adam to Noah. And Adam lived nine hundred and thirty (תתק\"ל) years; therefore Noah did not see him, but Lamekh his father did see him, for when Lamekh was born, Adam had eight hundred and seventy-four (תתע\"ד) years — so to complete the nine hundred and thirty (תתק\"ל) years that Adam lived, there are fifty-six (נ\"ו) years. Thus you see that Lamekh was fifty-six (נ\"ו) years old when he saw Adam the first man."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:37.347006374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}